# Scratch for anything that would otherwise land in /tmp, which on this machine
# is a 7.8 GB tmpfs on a 15 GB box — RAM. DuckDB's JDBC driver extracts a 58 MB
# native library into java.io.tmpdir on every JVM start (it deletes it on a
# GRACEFUL exit, so a killed run leaks one), and the browser harness makes a
# temp dir per server. Measured 2026-08-20: those filled /tmp to 100% mid-run
# and stopped the build, with 9,918 leaked fixture directories.
#
# Two earlier measurements were distorted by the same thing — the 2026-08-08
# Datahike/Datalevin benchmark ("on tmpfs it could not have been answered
# anyway") and phase 1's 10M-row gate, which had to use /var/tmp by hand.
#
# The .gitkeep is tracked on purpose: Java does not create java.io.tmpdir, so
# the directory has to exist on a fresh clone.
.tmp/*
!.tmp/.gitkeep

# SPIKE: compiled ClojureScript — build output, not source
resources/public/js/
.shadow-cljs/
